<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>Condition effects (descriptive)</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report mean SPICE (proportion YES) by experimental condition and tone, with the number of trials used per cell. These comparisons are descriptive and complement the exploratory sign tests.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5 </span>Robustness of the Confirmatory Effect</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Robustness checks for the confirmatory Tone<math id="S4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>SPICE effect show stability. Leave-one-interaction-out analyses preserved tone-wise SPICE ranges, and the Rao–Scott test stayed significant (with <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\text{adj}}&lt;.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>adj</mtext></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\text{adj}}&lt;.05</annotation></semantics></math>) in 100% of runs. A cluster bootstrap over interactions (<math id="S4.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1000</annotation></semantics></math>) produced tight distributions for Cramér’s V and the adjusted p-value.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 8</span>: </span><span id="S4.T8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">Condition <math id="S4.T8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> Tone: SPICE (YES) mean by preamble and format (descriptive).</span></figcaption>
